+## A throwing `beforeSession`
+
+A throw from `beforeSession` reaches the caller as a rejection, unchanged, and takes the same error path as any other failure in the turn: `onError` fires with that error, then `afterSession` fires ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+
+`afterSession` running after a failed `beforeSession` is deliberate: a deployer who allocates in `beforeSession` and releases in `afterSession` is not left holding the allocation on the path where it failed. A hook can assume that the turn was aborted before any provider interaction, so no tool ran, no model response was requested, and no assistant entry was written. A hook cannot tell from its arguments whether `beforeSession` finished its own allocation before it threw. A deployer who needs that distinction records it inside `beforeSession` itself, and treats `onError` as the signal that the turn failed.
+
